1
00:00:01,140 --> 00:00:07,000
[ARCHIVE AUDIO] Explosion at the main building, units 3 and 4.

2
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:08,300
Are there people there?

3
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:08,950
Yes.

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:15,630
At 1:23 and 40 seconds, the night shift pressed the emergency shutdown button.

5
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:18,490
Seconds later, Reactor Four blew apart.

6
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:24,760
Between that button and the moment Moscow told the world, 67 hours and 36 minutes went by.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,860
In those hours, a whole city was told to leave. Temporarily.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
[ARCHIVE AUDIO] "…to carry out a temporary evacuation…"

9
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:35,510
The first alarm outside the Soviet Union went off in Sweden.

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,200
[RECONSTRUCTION · SYNTHETIC AUDIO] An accident has occurred at the Chernobyl nuclear power station.

11
00:00:39,450 --> 00:00:41,900
One of the atomic reactors has been damaged.

12
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:44,770
And every one of those hours left a paper trail.
